From: Remora <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] monitor: inject only processes started as a zygote

The monitor takes every exec of /system/bin/app_process{64,32} by a child of init for a zygote
(restart), matching on /proc/<pid>/exe alone. On Android that binary also runs am, pm and cmd, and
Remora runs its in-image mirror agent as an init service through it. Each such exec is stopped and
handed to the injector, injection fails (the agent runs as shell and cannot open
/data/adb/modules/rezygisk/lib64/libzygisk.so: -13), the process is killed, init restarts it, and
after a few rounds should_stop_inject64() trips: "Zygote64 restart too much times, stop injecting",
"Stopped tracing init". From then on a real zygote restart comes up without Zygisk.

Observed on Remora's Android 17 image with the Play spoof stack (2026-11-16): the agent was killed
four times, five seconds apart, before the monitor gave up on init.

Require -Xzygote or --zygote among the exec'd process's arguments, which every zygote service in
AOSP passes, before treating it as one. When /proc/<pid>/cmdline cannot be read, the upstream
behaviour stands.

Applies on top of 0001.
---
--- a/loader/src/ptracer/monitor.c
+++ b/loader/src/ptracer/monitor.c
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 #include <errno.h>
 
 #include <unistd.h>
+#include <fcntl.h>
 #include <sys/epoll.h>
 #include <sys/signalfd.h>
 #include <sys/socket.h>
@@ -470,8 +471,36 @@
 #define APP_PROCESS_64 APP_PROCESS "64"
 #define APP_PROCESS_32 APP_PROCESS "32"
 
+/* REMORA: a zygote is an app_process whose arguments say so. Android's zygote services exec
+ * app_process with -Xzygote and --zygote; everything else that execs it is an ordinary program run
+ * through the same binary: am, pm and cmd, and Remora's in-image agent, an init service. Matching
+ * the program path alone takes each of those for a zygote restart: injection fails (an app_process
+ * running as shell cannot open the module's library), the process is killed, init restarts it,
+ * and after a few rounds the restart counter trips and the monitor stops tracing init for good, so
+ * the next real zygote restart comes up without Zygisk. When the arguments cannot be read, the
+ * upstream behaviour stands. */
+static bool is_zygote_exec(int pid) {
+  char path[64];
+  snprintf(path, sizeof(path), "/proc/%d/cmdline", pid);
+
+  int fd = open(path, O_RDONLY | O_CLOEXEC);
+  if (fd == -1) return true;
+
+  char args[4096];
+  ssize_t len = read(fd, args, sizeof(args) - 1);
+  close(fd);
+  if (len <= 0) return true;
+
+  args[len] = '\0';
+  for (ssize_t i = 0; i < len; i += (ssize_t)strlen(args + i) + 1) {
+    if (strcmp(args + i, "--zygote") == 0 || strcmp(args + i, "-Xzygote") == 0) return true;
+  }
+
+  return false;
+}
+
 #define PRE_INJECT(abi, is_64)                                        \
-  if (strcmp(program, APP_PROCESS_ ## abi) == 0) {                    \
+  if (strcmp(program, APP_PROCESS_ ## abi) == 0 && zygote_args) {     \
     tracer = "./bin/zygisk-ptrace" # abi;                             \
     is_tango = false;                                                 \
                                                                       \
@@ -691,6 +720,9 @@
 
           const char *tracer = NULL;
           bool is_tango = false;
+          const bool zygote_args = is_zygote_exec(pid);
+          if (!zygote_args && strncmp(program, APP_PROCESS, strlen(APP_PROCESS)) == 0)
+            LOGI("%d runs %s without --zygote: not a zygote, not injected", pid, program);
 
           do {
             if (tracing_state != TRACING) {
